  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1.13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IAtr">I Atr</ref> 1.13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.13" corresp="#wit-h">Gif him seo lad byrste, gylde þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> cynge his were, ⁊ sy se man útlah.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="1.13" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf him seo lad byrste, gylde ðam cynge his were, ⁊ si se man utlah.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="1.13" corresp="#wit-q">Si lada frangat ei, reddat regi weram suam, et sit homo forsbannitus apud omnes (homines).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="1.13" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf him seo lad byrste, gylde ðam cynge his were ⁊ si se man utlah.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If he fails to clear himself, he shall pay his [own] wergeld to the king, and the man shall be an outlaw.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn ihm diese Reinigung misslingt, zahle er dem König sein Wergeld. Und jener [Untergebene] sei friedlos.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If this clearing fails him, let him pay the king his wergild. And let that [dependant] be an outlaw.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="219"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-9a">I Atr 1.9a</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. 1, 9a</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_31-2">II Cn 31.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares I Atr 1.9a.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
